{"change_summary":"Implemented the three pending helper-layer amendments. Added explicit unit/basis guidance to `monod_rate` and `monod_factor` in `nitrogen_cycle.rs`, documented that substrate displacement currently assumes 100% water exclusion / 0% porosity, and removed the geometry/state naming collision by renaming the gross-volume APIs on `TankGeometry` to `gross_water_volume_l`, `surface_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`, and `wall_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`. Updated all affected runtime call sites, regression tests, and repo docs/spec references to the renamed gross-volume API so `TankState::water_volume_l()` remains the only public bare `water_volume_l` semantic.","outstanding_risks":["Substrate displacement is still modeled as 100% solid / 0% porosity; this pass only documented that assumption, so future substrate-physics work can still retune net-water calculations once porosity is represented explicitly.","The geometry-side gross-volume API rename (`gross_water_volume_l`, `surface_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`, `wall_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`) is source-breaking for any downstream callers outside this workspace that still reference the old method names.","Legacy process field names such as `plant_half_saturation_n_mg_total` and `aob_k_tan_mg` still read like total-mass parameters even though runtime semantics are now concentration- or area-normalized; that rename work remains deferred to downstream normalization beads."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspected the current geometry, save-migration, TUI, scenario-test, and nitrogen-cycle code paths to confirm the remaining gaps: missing Monod unit guidance, undocumented full-displacement semantics, and the conflicting gross-vs-net `water_volume_l()` API names.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Added the requested helper documentation by annotating `monod_rate` and `monod_factor` with same-units guidance and documenting that `substrate_displacement_l` / `water_volume_l_with_substrate_depth` currently assume 100% displacement because substrate porosity is not modeled yet.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Renamed the geometry-side gross helpers to `gross_water_volume_l`, `surface_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`, and `wall_area_to_gross_volume_ratio`, then updated save migration, the startup summary, affected regression tests, and the relevant docs/spec references so only `TankState::water_volume_l()` keeps the bare canonical name.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Ran formatting, full workspace validation, and a source scan to confirm the workspace is clean and that the old geometry-side bare `water_volume_l` / gross-ratio names no longer remain.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all` completed successfully.","`cargo fmt --all --check` completed successfully.","`cargo test --quiet` completed successfully across the workspace.","`cargo clippy --all-targets --quiet` completed successfully.","`rg -n \"geometry\\.water_volume_l\\(|pub fn water_volume_l\\(&self\\) -> f64|surface_area_to_volume_ratio|wall_area_to_volume_ratio\" crates docs spec.md -g'*.rs' -g'*.md'` now reports only `TankState::water_volume_l()` as the remaining public bare `water_volume_l` API.","Updated the affected documentation and regression call sites to the renamed gross-volume API in `docs/UNITS.md`, `spec.md`, `crates/tank_core/tests/*`, `crates/tank_scenarios/tests/materialization.rs`, and `crates/tank_tui/src/main.rs`.","No `.beads/` files changed in this remediation pass, so `br lint` was not required."]}